      <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
           EDITORIAL INDEPENDENCE
      ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
      <section class="meth-section" id="editorial-independence">
        <h2>Editorial Independence & Affiliate Disclosure</h2>
        <p>Eastern Alignment earns commissions when visitors sign up for or purchase through certain links on this site (including links to Kasamba, Purple Garden, and Keen). This is the economic model that funds the site, the testing, and the ongoing research.</p>

        <p>Here is how we prevent that relationship from compromising the work:</p>

        <ul class="independence-list">
          <li><strong>Scoring dimensions and weights are fixed before testing begins.</strong> They are documented on this page. A platform cannot negotiate its weight distribution.</li>
          <li><strong>A higher commission does not produce a higher score.</strong> We have rated platforms with lower affiliate payouts above platforms with higher payouts — our current rankings reflect this.</li>
          <li><strong>We do not accept payment for rankings, placements, or favorable coverage.</strong> No platform can buy a higher position.</li>
          <li><strong>We do not accept free readings in exchange for coverage.</strong> Every session we reference was paid for at standard consumer rates.</li>
          <li><strong>No platform reviews or approves our content before publication.</strong> Platforms see our reviews when the public does.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>We disclose the affiliate relationship on every page that contains affiliate links, in the <a href="/disclosure/">site-wide disclosure</a>, and here. The relationship is real, the firewall is real, and both are visible.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
           WHAT WE DON'T DO
      ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
      <section class="meth-section" id="what-we-dont-do">
        <h2>What We Explicitly Do Not Do</h2>
        <div class="dont-list card">
          <ul>
            <li>We don't accept payment for rankings or editorial placements.</li>
            <li>We don't accept free readings in exchange for favorable coverage.</li>
            <li>We don't fabricate sessions or firsthand experiences.</li>
            <li>We don't rewrite platform marketing copy and present it as independent testing.</li>
            <li>We don't treat user testimonials as proof of psychic ability.</li>
            <li>We don't suppress negative findings because a platform pays a higher commission.</li>
            <li>We don't allow any platform to review or approve our content before publication.</li>
            <li>We don't claim to measure "psychic accuracy" as a scientific quantity.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
           LIMITS OF OUR METHOD
      ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
      <section class="meth-section" id="limitations">
        <h2>Limits of Our Method</h2>
        <p>Intellectual honesty requires acknowledging what our methodology cannot do. These are structural limitations, not failures of effort:</p>

        <ul class="limitations-list">
          <li><strong>A personal reading experience is not a controlled experiment.</strong> Our sessions are real, but they are not double-blinded studies. We mitigate bias through structured rubrics and multi-reader sampling, but cannot eliminate subjectivity entirely.</li>
          <li><strong>Small samples have statistical limitations.</strong> Testing a sample of readers on a platform with 500+ does not capture every possible experience. We are explicit about the fact that our coverage is a sample, not a census.</li>
          <li><strong>A positive session does not prove supernatural ability.</strong> A reader may deliver strikingly accurate insights through skill, cold reading, pattern recognition, genuine intuition, or some combination. We evaluate information quality, not metaphysical mechanism.</li>
          <li><strong>A negative session does not condemn an entire platform.</strong> Connection quality varies. We counterbalance this by sampling multiple readers across different conditions.</li>
          <li><strong>Platform policies and pricing change.</strong> Our documentation reflects conditions at the time of testing. We update when we learn of material changes, but there is always a lag between platform changes and our verification.</li>
          <li><strong>Outcome tracking cannot eliminate coincidence or hindsight bias.</strong> When a prediction appears to "come true," we note it but do not treat it as scientific proof. When one doesn't, we note that too.</li>
          <li><strong>We are one person, not a testing laboratory.</strong> Eastern Alignment is researched, tested, written, and maintained by <a href="/about/">Sarah</a> — not a team of anonymous staff writers. This means deeper expertise but narrower throughput.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>These limitations are not caveats designed to protect us legally. They are honest boundaries on what any individual reviewer can credibly claim — and respecting them is what separates a methodology from marketing.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
           DATA COLLECTION — FIRSTHAND vs. SECONDHAND
      ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
      <section class="meth-section" id="data-sources">
        <h2>Firsthand Testing vs. Aggregated Research</h2>
        <p>We separate our data sources clearly so you always know what is direct experience and what is synthesized research. This is not a caveat — it is an integrity requirement.</p>

        <div class="data-source-grid">
          <div class="data-source-card card">
            <h4>🔬 Firsthand Testing (Level A Evidence)</h4>
            <p>Content produced from our own paid sessions, our own platform interactions, and our own documented observations. Platform reviews incorporate firsthand testing data where available; reader assessments combine direct observation with verified public data.</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted">Identifiable by: specific session details, documented spending, named readers, timestamps, and references to transcripts or session notes.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="data-source-card card">
            <h4>📊 Aggregated Research (Level B–C Evidence)</h4>
            <p>Content synthesized from verified platform data, community user experiences, public reviews, and AI-assisted information processing. Most <strong>guides and comparisons</strong> combine firsthand testing data with aggregated research.</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted">Identifiable by: references to "user reports," "community sentiment," or "based on platform data." We do not present aggregated research as personal testing.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

